  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed system changes driven by the private sector in Northern Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project serves to fund a data collection scientific study conducted by SeedNL, Wageningen University and Research (WUR) and WorldVeg regarding the socioeconomic impact of the adoption of improved vegetable varieties and good agricultural practices as promoted by Dutch-funded interventions in Northern Nigeria (Kano and Kaduna), with a focus on the SDGP project of East-West Seed (EWS). The study would serve as a scientific contribution to and underpinning of, the Netherlands-Nigeria Seed Partnership (NNSP) and SeedNL. Moreover, findings can be used to improve future private-sector development projects focused on seed sector development.</narrative>
  </description>
